<!--
  Robot configuration for the BIOBUZZ launcher bench.

  THIS IS NOT A ROBOT. It is a spare Control Hub with the real launcher on
  it: the two flywheel modules and the feeder, before they are bolted to a
  chassis. It exists so the launcher's numbers (which wheel is reversed, the
  speed each piece leaves at, how long the feeder runs) can be found at a
  bench while the build team has the robots.

  Like the robot configs, it ships inside the APK and appears in the Driver
  Station list as "robot_launcher_bench" as soon as the app is installed. The
  one manual step, once per hub: on the bench's Driver Station,
  Configure Robot -> robot_launcher_bench -> Activate. The Launcher Bench
  OpMode warns if some other configuration is active.

  WIRING: the same motor numbers as the robots, so a number found here is a
  number for the robot. On the robots these three sit on the Expansion Hub;
  here there is only a Control Hub, so they sit on its motor ports.
    launcher_left   motor port 1, its encoder in encoder port 1
    launcher_right  motor port 2, its encoder in encoder port 2
    feeder          motor port 3 (encoder optional; the feeder runs on power)
  Both encoders must be plugged in: the launcher holds speed with the hub's
  velocity loop, and a wheel with no encoder reads 0 and is cut by the code.

  Device names here must match org.firstinspires.ftc.teamcode.hardware.DeviceNames
  (the LAUNCHER_BENCH list). RobotConfigXmlTest fails the build if they disagree.
-->
<Robot type="FirstInspires-FTC">
    <LynxUsbDevice name="Control Hub Portal" serialNumber="(embedded)" parentModuleAddress="173">
        <LynxModule name="Control Hub" port="173">

            <!-- The launcher, on the robots' motor numbers. -->
            <goBILDA5202SeriesMotor name="launcher_left"  port="1" />
            <goBILDA5202SeriesMotor name="launcher_right" port="2" />
            <goBILDA5202SeriesMotor name="feeder"         port="3" />

        </LynxModule>
    </LynxUsbDevice>
</Robot>
